From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 11:48:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] apprt: ghostty_surface_render_now for embedders without a
 paint loop

An embedder that feeds pty output has no way to say "I just gave you
bytes, put them on screen". queueRender goes through the renderer's
coalescing wakeup, and an update landing after the render thread has
sampled terminal state is folded into a wake that has already done its
work - so the tail of a burst never reaches the screen and the surface
sits stale until some unrelated event forces a render.

ghostty_surface_draw is not that lever: it is drawFrame alone, which
re-presents the cells the render thread last *built*. Forcing it after
new output redraws stale content - measured, the pane still froze.

renderNow does both halves, updateFrame then drawFrame, on the calling
thread. Both take the renderer state mutex exactly as the render thread's
own path does, so it is safe from the thread feeding output.

This only shows up without a paint loop. hwnd-host calls
ghostty_surface_draw on WM_PAINT and a focused surface gets one-shot
renders from focus, scroll and visibility changes - which is why three
phases of harness work never surfaced it, and why an unfocused pane in a
XAML SwapChainPanel surfaced it immediately.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012ee27Fih3vSPYsqrUBpUoc
---
 include/ghostty.h      | 11 +++++++++++
 src/Surface.zig        | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/apprt/embedded.zig | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 55 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/ghostty.h b/include/ghostty.h
index 166d93699..b316451ae 100644
--- a/include/ghostty.h
+++ b/include/ghostty.h
@@ -1227,6 +1227,17 @@ GHOSTTY_API bool ghostty_surface_needs_confirm_quit(ghostty_surface_t);
 GHOSTTY_API bool ghostty_surface_process_exited(ghostty_surface_t);
 GHOSTTY_API void ghostty_surface_refresh(ghostty_surface_t);
 GHOSTTY_API void ghostty_surface_draw(ghostty_surface_t);
+// Rebuild the frame from current terminal state and draw it immediately, on
+// the calling thread.
+//
+// For embedders that feed pty output and have no paint loop.
+// ghostty_surface_draw only re-presents the cells the render thread last
+// built; this rebuilds them first, so bytes just written with
+// ghostty_surface_write_pty_output actually reach the screen instead of
+// waiting for an unrelated event (focus, scroll, resize) to force a render.
+//
+// Safe to call from the thread feeding output.
+GHOSTTY_API void ghostty_surface_render_now(ghostty_surface_t);
 GHOSTTY_API void ghostty_surface_set_content_scale(ghostty_surface_t, double, double);
 GHOSTTY_API void ghostty_surface_set_focus(ghostty_surface_t, bool);
 GHOSTTY_API void ghostty_surface_set_occlusion(ghostty_surface_t, bool);
diff --git a/src/Surface.zig b/src/Surface.zig
index c61f258df..4e6bd96eb 100644
--- a/src/Surface.zig
+++ b/src/Surface.zig
@@ -905,6 +905,29 @@ pub fn draw(self: *Surface) !void {
     try self.renderer.drawFrame(true);
 }
 
+/// Rebuild the frame from the current terminal state and draw it, now, on
+/// the calling thread.
+///
+/// `draw` only re-presents the cells the render thread last built, which is
+/// what a resize needs. An embedder that has just pushed pty output needs the
+/// other half too: without the rebuild it re-presents stale content.
+///
+/// This exists because scheduling a render is not sufficient for an embedder
+/// whose surface is not driven by a paint loop. `queueRender` goes through the
+/// renderer's coalescing wakeup, and an update landing after the render thread
+/// has sampled terminal state is folded into a wake that has already done its
+/// work - so the last output of a burst never reaches the screen and the
+/// surface sits stale until some unrelated event (focus, scroll, visibility)
+/// forces a render. A terminal in a XAML SwapChainPanel has no paint loop to
+/// hide that.
+///
+/// Both halves take the renderer state mutex, the same as the render thread's
+/// own path, so calling this from the thread feeding output is safe.
+pub fn renderNow(self: *Surface) !void {
+    try self.renderer.updateFrame(&self.renderer_state, true);
+    try self.renderer.drawFrame(true);
+}
+
 /// Activate the inspector. This will begin collecting inspection data.
 /// This will not affect the GUI. The GUI must use performAction to
 /// show/hide the inspector UI.
diff --git a/src/apprt/embedded.zig b/src/apprt/embedded.zig
index 7c5bfb53f..ac4c943cf 100644
--- a/src/apprt/embedded.zig
+++ b/src/apprt/embedded.zig
@@ -930,6 +930,13 @@ pub const Surface = struct {
         };
     }
 
+    pub fn renderNow(self: *Surface) void {
+        self.core_surface.renderNow() catch |err| {
+            log.err("error in renderNow err={}", .{err});
+            return;
+        };
+    }
+
     pub fn updateContentScale(self: *Surface, x: f64, y: f64) void {
         // We are an embedded API so the caller can send us all sorts of
         // garbage. We want to make sure that the float values are valid
@@ -1943,6 +1950,20 @@ pub const CAPI = struct {
         surface.draw();
     }
 
+    /// Rebuild the frame from current terminal state and draw it immediately,
+    /// on the calling thread.
+    ///
+    /// For embedders that feed pty output and have no paint loop to fall back
+    /// on. ghostty_surface_draw only re-presents the cells the render thread
+    /// last built; this rebuilds them first, so output that has just been
+    /// written with ghostty_surface_write_pty_output actually reaches the
+    /// screen rather than waiting for an unrelated event to force a render.
+    ///
+    /// Safe to call from the thread feeding output.
+    export fn ghostty_surface_render_now(surface: *Surface) void {
+        surface.renderNow();
+    }
+
     /// Update the size of a surface. This will trigger resize notifications
     /// to the pty and the renderer.
     export fn ghostty_surface_set_size(surface: *Surface, w: u32, h: u32) void {
